    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SlopeCycle Interview Agent (v2: event-driven)\nThere is **no timer**. This workflow runs only when something rings its **doorbell**: a new interview was sent, the Mac woke up, or someone pressed **Run now** on the status page.\n\nThen: ask the processor what is waiting, let it analyse each interview **one at a time**, save the answers to the Google Sheet, **read them back from the sheet**, and let the processor compare. Only a perfect match lets it delete the interview.\n\n**n8n only moves things around. The processor decides everything.** Before first use: open **Settings** and paste your Sheet id.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "3f6b0a9b-8a1a-5dbf-8ed5-034a162bd159",
      "name": "Note: Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -440
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. The doorbell\nOne web address, POST `/webhook/slopecycle-run`. It answers right away and carries no data: it only says *go and look*. Listens on this Mac only.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 280,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "f1e3c31b-55da-50a1-be01-758d3ea24b99",
      "name": "Note: 1 Doorbell",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Settings\nThe Sheet id and the processor address. Change them here and nowhere else.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 280,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "93b1e398-3ca8-5c40-9ba3-53c9f4e6c09c",
      "name": "Note: 2 Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        280,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. What is waiting?\nThe processor refreshes the queue, tidies up anything already verified, and lists what to do. Nothing waiting means nothing happens.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "bd6f8a13-a9b7-55f6-b866-293a5877d300",
      "name": "Note: 3 Ask",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        580,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4. One interview at a time\nThe processor runs one local AI model, so interviews go one by one. Audio can take up to an hour. The processor does the reading, thinking and checking, and hands back ready-to-save rows.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 780,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "7431ac21-1306-583d-ba35-a1a208e21591",
      "name": "Note: 4 Loop",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 5. Save to the Google Sheet\nIn order: **Evidence**, **Interviews**, then **Run Log**. Each row is matched on its id, so sending it twice never makes a copy. Empty lists are skipped. Cells are saved exactly as given (RAW), so dates stay text and nothing is ever treated as a formula.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 2600,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "827e9139-2233-50fc-a562-fbb9fc4daca9",
      "name": "Note: 5 Save",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1880,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 6. Read it back from the sheet (Interviews)\nThe rows are fetched again from the **sheet itself** by their id. This is the real check: it proves the sheet holds the data.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 1440,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "52edb5fa-f03f-5eaa-b206-c521c7361192",
      "name": "Note: 6a Read Interviews",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4540,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Read it back (Evidence quotes)\nEvery quote for this interview is fetched, **all matches**, not only the first.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 1440,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "ea22e8bf-d604-58d2-ae78-454e56871610",
      "name": "Note: 6b Read Evidence",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        6100,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Read it back (Run Log)\nEvery interview has a Run Log row, even duplicates and failures, so this always runs.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "6e8643dd-ac4a-59fd-8daf-fc8019f6f741",
      "name": "Note: 6c Read Run Log",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        7660,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 7. Let the processor compare\nThe three tabs go to the processor in one package. It checks every cell. Match: it deletes the interview. No match: it keeps it and tries again later.",
        "height": 660,
        "width": 540,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "488f65f9-6afa-54f5-8d47-bd586cbfcccc",
      "name": "Note: 7 Compare",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        8180,
        -140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Nothing is deleted until the sheet is read back and matches\nThe processor never trusts \"the save worked\". It keeps its own copy of what it sent, and only deletes the interview (notes and recording) from the private queue after it receives rows **read back from the Google Sheet** that match, cell for cell.\n- Missing row, missing column or changed value: **not deleted**, saved again on the next run.\n- Sheet save or read fails: the processor is told, and keeps everything.\n- Failed interviews (unreadable audio, empty notes) are never deleted automatically.\n- n8n keeps **no copy** of the interview content (execution history is switched off).",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 1900,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "4b214b22-fbfd-5930-a5ba-3bcd1a727f10",
      "name": "Note: Safety",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4540,
        -440
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "If processing an interview fails, or any Google Sheets step fails, we skip to the next interview. A sheet failure is reported to the processor (**Tell processor: sheet failed**), which keeps the data and offers it again later.",
        "height": 150,
        "width": 2600,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "a104f039-f03a-5e73-85c1-0313c448260d",
      "name": "Note: Failures",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1880,
        540
      ]
    }
  ],
